{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "02NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$f : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$X'$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-modification}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7260f777032b66b51adfe3a36dfdc9aabea6721cd1a07dea533db76c03aa4914", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0080ac07e68c22e4a137ddad6fe998dd0d5e92e4cf1485e74c8786a0577ad747", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an integral scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>modification of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis a birational proper morphism <MATH_0003> with <MATH_0004>\nintegral.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cff07649f746ada6934370dbe9adf6ca8298452dff32c0e38aba303ddb9821ba", "unit_id": "tag:0AAZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$f^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "MATH_0005": "$f^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$X'$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$1$", "MATH_0010": "$f^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "MATH_0011": "$1$", "MATH_0012": "$f : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$f^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "MATH_0014": "$U \\subset X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-degree}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{proposition-generic-flatness}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-finite-flat}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:66f53f21c2367fea37afa8a6d45063b553fcf35d5fb6e2712adc98cfde534464", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ce7adc6307ae06520485fee46cd7600779cdbbba0849c7b45a3308509af8cc98", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a modification as in the definition. By\nLemma <REF_0001> there exists a nonempty <MATH_0002> such\nthat <MATH_0003> is finite. By generic flatness\n(Proposition <REF_0002>)\nwe may assume <MATH_0004> is flat and of finite presentation.\nSo <MATH_0005> is finite locally free (Lemma <REF_0003>).\nSince <MATH_0006> is birational, the degree of <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008> is <MATH_0009>.\nHence <MATH_0010> is finite locally free of degree <MATH_0011>,\nin other words it is an isomorphism. Thus we can <TEXTITOPEN_0001>redefine<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> a\nmodification to be a proper morphism <MATH_0012> of integral schemes\nsuch that <MATH_0013> is an isomorphism for some nonempty open\n<MATH_0014>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:72a1359900338f1b23680c175fc8ec90042e4f3a510f5fe910305c485efb5873", "unit_id": "tag:02NV:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "02NV", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[Definition 2.20]{alterations}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$f : Y \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$f^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\subset X$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-alteration}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c22e3200d1d9ffa37856cdafb83da533092f5340cf4c8c7e6fc7594e96f8f794", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:12faaf2c6cb17089684bd29295a6186e31cba39b8ca4f5a6f8a9076c11ac4476", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an integral scheme. An <TEXTITOPEN_0001>alteration of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis a proper dominant morphism <MATH_0003> with <MATH_0004> integral such\nthat <MATH_0005> is finite for some nonempty open <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:91f9d92dfb44515f5f3b3a27ce5f3e9483d2a47275fbe0bc8d3e2fd47cff6cd9", "unit_id": "tag:0AB0:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$f : Y \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\cite{alterations}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-degree}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d15512fb4017c3bd46d03203bfedf3a324ed21cb63dc96182fd6225445a0cf89", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d60b35873cc6959b17966703926794c0d240b214e2333d12ce2a24e2e1757c7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is the definition as given in <REF_0001>, except that\nhere we do not require <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> to be Noetherian. Arguing as above\nwe see that an alteration is a proper dominant morphism <MATH_0003>\nof integral schemes which induces a finite extension of\nfunction fields, i.e., such that the equivalent conditions of\nLemma <REF_0002> hold.\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:261ee454f22cc20be22a013b90484c9fb9d728823b1a7f04c5a1aac13fe49c45", "unit_id": "tag:02NV:prose-0004"}
